From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:16:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Make its own copies and clears with a context state of
 its own.

A drawing surface's tiles are copied and cleared, and a texture is
mirrored to the device a target draws with, through the immediate
context of the application's device.  With a state of the application's
active that emulates ID3D10Device, as Office's D3D10.1 device has, those
calls are dropped; they now go through a state of our own, kept with
the graphics device or the mirror and made again for another device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

